const Q_R_MODELO1_DEV = [
  ["Teste · Modelo 1", "M1.11a", "<b>P. 11 (4,5 valores)</b> Rede com comutação de pacotes <i>store-and-forward</i>: <b>T1 —LAN— R1 —WAN— T2</b>. Pacotes de 1000 Bytes (com cabeçalhos) de T1 para T2. Ambas as ligações em fibra (propagação a 2×10<sup>8</sup> m/s). A LAN tem 20 m e 10 Mbit/s. Na WAN, o atraso de propagação é 15 ms e o de transmissão é 0,6 ms.<br><br>(a) Calcula os atrasos de transmissão e de propagação na LAN.", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p><strong>Significado de todas as variáveis e abreviações do problema:</strong> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Length</em> = tamanho do pacote)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> Bytes</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8000</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1000\\text{ Bytes} = 1000 \\times 8\\text{ bits} = 8000\\text{ bits} = 8\\times 10^3\\text{ b}</annotation></semantics></math>. <em>(Atenção: 1 Byte tem 8 bits; as contas de transmissão usam sempre bits, nunca Bytes!).</em> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_{LAN}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Rate</em> = taxa de transmissão / capacidade da ligação LAN)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> Mbit/s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bit/s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b/s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">10\\text{ Mbit/s} = 10 \\times 10^6\\text{ bit/s} = 10^7\\text{ b/s}</annotation></semantics></math>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">l_{LAN}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>length</em> = comprimento físico do cabo da LAN)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>20</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> metros</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">20\\text{ metros}</annotation></semantics></math>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>velocity</em> = velocidade de propagação da luz no meio físico)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\times 10^8\\text{ m/s}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(valor típico da velocidade da luz dentro do núcleo de fibra ótica)</em>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>transmission delay</em> = atraso de transmissão)</strong>: tempo que a placa de rede demora a “injetar” (empurrar) todos os bits do pacote para o cabo. Fórmula: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans} = L / R</annotation></semantics></math>. <em>(Depende do tamanho do pacote <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</annotation></semantics></math> e da taxa <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math>; não depende da distância!).</em> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>propagation delay</em> = atraso de propagação)</strong>: tempo que o sinal eletromagnético demora a percorrer fisicamente o cabo da origem ao destino à velocidade da luz. Fórmula: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">distância</mtext><mi>/</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop} = \\text{distância} / v</annotation></semantics></math>. <em>(Depende da distância e do meio; não depende do tamanho do pacote!).</em> * <strong>Dados da ligação WAN (já calculados e fornecidos no enunciado):</strong> * <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,WAN} = 0{,}6\\text{ ms} = 6\\times 10^{-4}\\text{ s}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(atraso de transmissão na WAN)</em>. * <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop,WAN} = 15\\text{ ms} = 1{,}5\\times 10^{-2}\\text{ s}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(atraso de propagação na WAN)</em>.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><p><strong>Atraso de transmissão na LAN (<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,LAN}</annotation></semantics></math>)</strong> — tempo para injetar os 8000 bits no cabo da LAN a 10 Mbps: <math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> (tamanho do pacote em bits)</mtext></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> (capacidade em bit/s)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b</mtext></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟖</mn><mo mathvariant=\"bold\">×</mo><msup><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟏𝟎</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold-italic\">−</mi><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟒</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"bold\"> 𝐬</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟎</mn><mo mathvariant=\"bold\">,</mo><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟖</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"bold\"> 𝐦𝐬</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,LAN} = \\frac{L\\text{ (tamanho do pacote em bits)}}{R_{LAN}\\text{ (capacidade em bit/s)}} = \\frac{8\\times10^3\\text{ b}}{10^7\\text{ b/s}} = \\mathbf{8\\times10^{-4}\\text{ s}} = \\mathbf{0{,}8\\text{ ms}}</annotation></semantics></math></p></li>\n<li><p><strong>Atraso de propagação na LAN (<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop,LAN}</annotation></semantics></math>)</strong> — tempo para a luz percorrer os 20 metros de cabo: <math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> (distância em metros)</mtext></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> (velocidade da luz em m/s)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> m</mtext></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟏𝟎</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold-italic\">−</mi><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟕</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"bold\"> 𝐬</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟎</mn><mo mathvariant=\"bold\">,</mo><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟏</mn><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"bold-italic\">𝝁</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold-italic\">𝒔</mi></mrow><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> (microssegundos)</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop,LAN} = \\frac{l_{LAN}\\text{ (distância em metros)}}{v\\text{ (velocidade da luz em m/s)}} = \\frac{20\\text{ m}}{2\\times10^8\\text{ m/s}} = \\mathbf{10^{-7}\\text{ s}} = \\mathbf{0{,}1\\ \\mu s}\\text{ (microssegundos)}</annotation></semantics></math></p></li>\n</ol>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> d<sub>trans</sub> = L/R; d<sub>prop</sub> = d/v.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#as-quatro-fontes-de-atraso\" target=\"_blank\">📖 As quatro fontes de atraso</a>"],
  ["Teste · Modelo 1", "M1.11b", "<b>P. 11 (4,5 valores)</b> Rede com comutação de pacotes <i>store-and-forward</i>: <b>T1 —LAN— R1 —WAN— T2</b>. Pacotes de 1000 Bytes (com cabeçalhos) de T1 para T2. Ambas as ligações em fibra (propagação a 2×10<sup>8</sup> m/s). A LAN tem 20 m e 10 Mbit/s. Na WAN, o atraso de propagação é 15 ms e o de transmissão é 0,6 ms.<br><br>(b) Quanto demora a enviar <b>um</b> pacote de T1 para T2 (processamento desprezável, filas vazias)?", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p><strong>Significado de todas as variáveis e abreviações do problema:</strong> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Length</em> = tamanho do pacote)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> Bytes</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8000</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1000\\text{ Bytes} = 1000 \\times 8\\text{ bits} = 8000\\text{ bits} = 8\\times 10^3\\text{ b}</annotation></semantics></math>. <em>(Atenção: 1 Byte tem 8 bits; as contas de transmissão usam sempre bits, nunca Bytes!).</em> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_{LAN}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Rate</em> = taxa de transmissão / capacidade da ligação LAN)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> Mbit/s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bit/s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b/s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">10\\text{ Mbit/s} = 10 \\times 10^6\\text{ bit/s} = 10^7\\text{ b/s}</annotation></semantics></math>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">l_{LAN}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>length</em> = comprimento físico do cabo da LAN)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>20</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> metros</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">20\\text{ metros}</annotation></semantics></math>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>velocity</em> = velocidade de propagação da luz no meio físico)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\times 10^8\\text{ m/s}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(valor típico da velocidade da luz dentro do núcleo de fibra ótica)</em>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>transmission delay</em> = atraso de transmissão)</strong>: tempo que a placa de rede demora a “injetar” (empurrar) todos os bits do pacote para o cabo. Fórmula: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans} = L / R</annotation></semantics></math>. <em>(Depende do tamanho do pacote <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</annotation></semantics></math> e da taxa <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math>; não depende da distância!).</em> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>propagation delay</em> = atraso de propagação)</strong>: tempo que o sinal eletromagnético demora a percorrer fisicamente o cabo da origem ao destino à velocidade da luz. Fórmula: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">distância</mtext><mi>/</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop} = \\text{distância} / v</annotation></semantics></math>. <em>(Depende da distância e do meio; não depende do tamanho do pacote!).</em> * <strong>Dados da ligação WAN (já calculados e fornecidos no enunciado):</strong> * <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,WAN} = 0{,}6\\text{ ms} = 6\\times 10^{-4}\\text{ s}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(atraso de transmissão na WAN)</em>. * <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop,WAN} = 15\\text{ ms} = 1{,}5\\times 10^{-2}\\text{ s}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(atraso de propagação na WAN)</em>.</p>\n<p><strong>Princípio de <em>Store-and-forward</em> (armazenar e reenviar):</strong> o router R1 só começa a transmitir o pacote para a WAN <strong>depois de o ter recebido por completo</strong> da LAN (o último bit do pacote tem de estar guardado na memória do router).</p>\n<p>Como não há filas de espera nem atrasos de processamento nodais, o percurso de um único pacote soma as 4 parcelas cronológicas: 1. <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,LAN}</annotation></semantics></math>: T1 injeta todos os bits na LAN (<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0{,}8\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math>). 2. <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop,LAN}</annotation></semantics></math>: os bits viajam fisicamente pela fibra da LAN até chegarem a R1 (<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0001</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0{,}0001\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math>). 3. <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,WAN}</annotation></semantics></math>: R1 injeta todos os bits na WAN (<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0{,}6\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math>). 4. <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop,WAN}</annotation></semantics></math>: os bits viajam fisicamente pela fibra da WAN até chegarem a T2 (<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>15</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">15\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{total,1} = d_{trans,LAN} + d_{prop,LAN} + d_{trans,WAN} + d_{prop,WAN}</annotation></semantics></math> <math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0001</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟏𝟔</mn><mo mathvariant=\"bold\">,</mo><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟒𝟎𝟎𝟏</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"bold\"> 𝐦𝐬</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">= 0{,}8\\text{ ms} + 0{,}0001\\text{ ms} + 0{,}6\\text{ ms} + 15\\text{ ms} = \\mathbf{16{,}4001\\text{ ms}} \\approx 16{,}4\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> um pacote: soma trans + prop de cada ligação.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#as-quatro-fontes-de-atraso\" target=\"_blank\">📖 As quatro fontes de atraso</a>"],
  ["Teste · Modelo 1", "M1.11c", "<b>P. 11 (4,5 valores)</b> Rede com comutação de pacotes <i>store-and-forward</i>: <b>T1 —LAN— R1 —WAN— T2</b>. Pacotes de 1000 Bytes (com cabeçalhos) de T1 para T2. Ambas as ligações em fibra (propagação a 2×10<sup>8</sup> m/s). A LAN tem 20 m e 10 Mbit/s. Na WAN, o atraso de propagação é 15 ms e o de transmissão é 0,6 ms.<br><br>(c) Desenha o diagrama temporal (T1, R1, T2 com o tempo a descer) do envio de <b>4 pacotes</b>, nas condições da alínea anterior. Faz no papel e compara.", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p><strong>Significado de todas as variáveis e abreviações do problema:</strong> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Length</em> = tamanho do pacote)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> Bytes</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8000</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1000\\text{ Bytes} = 1000 \\times 8\\text{ bits} = 8000\\text{ bits} = 8\\times 10^3\\text{ b}</annotation></semantics></math>. <em>(Atenção: 1 Byte tem 8 bits; as contas de transmissão usam sempre bits, nunca Bytes!).</em> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_{LAN}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Rate</em> = taxa de transmissão / capacidade da ligação LAN)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> Mbit/s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bit/s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b/s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">10\\text{ Mbit/s} = 10 \\times 10^6\\text{ bit/s} = 10^7\\text{ b/s}</annotation></semantics></math>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">l_{LAN}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>length</em> = comprimento físico do cabo da LAN)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>20</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> metros</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">20\\text{ metros}</annotation></semantics></math>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>velocity</em> = velocidade de propagação da luz no meio físico)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\times 10^8\\text{ m/s}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(valor típico da velocidade da luz dentro do núcleo de fibra ótica)</em>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>transmission delay</em> = atraso de transmissão)</strong>: tempo que a placa de rede demora a “injetar” (empurrar) todos os bits do pacote para o cabo. Fórmula: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans} = L / R</annotation></semantics></math>. <em>(Depende do tamanho do pacote <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</annotation></semantics></math> e da taxa <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math>; não depende da distância!).</em> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>propagation delay</em> = atraso de propagação)</strong>: tempo que o sinal eletromagnético demora a percorrer fisicamente o cabo da origem ao destino à velocidade da luz. Fórmula: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">distância</mtext><mi>/</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop} = \\text{distância} / v</annotation></semantics></math>. <em>(Depende da distância e do meio; não depende do tamanho do pacote!).</em> * <strong>Dados da ligação WAN (já calculados e fornecidos no enunciado):</strong> * <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,WAN} = 0{,}6\\text{ ms} = 6\\times 10^{-4}\\text{ s}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(atraso de transmissão na WAN)</em>. * <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop,WAN} = 15\\text{ ms} = 1{,}5\\times 10^{-2}\\text{ s}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(atraso de propagação na WAN)</em>.</p>\n<p><img src=\"assets/guia-redes/sol_m1_store_forward.svg\" alt=\"4 pacotes de T1 a T2: a LAN (0,8 ms por pacote) é a ligação mais lenta, por isso nunca há fila em R1\" /></p>\n<p><strong>Como ler e construir o diagrama temporal:</strong> * O eixo vertical representa o <strong>tempo a avançar para baixo</strong>. * A largura de cada faixa representa o atraso de transmissão <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans}</annotation></semantics></math> (tempo gasto a emitir o pacote). * A inclinação de cada faixa representa o atraso de propagação <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop}</annotation></semantics></math> (tempo de viagem no cabo). * Na LAN, a propagação é minúscula (<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0001</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0{,}1\\ \\mu\\text{s} = 0{,}0001\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math>), pelo que as faixas parecem quase horizontais. * Na WAN, a propagação é grande (<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>15</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">15\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math>), pelo que as faixas descem bastante. * <strong>Porque não há fila no router R1?</strong> A LAN despacha 1 pacote a cada <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0{,}8\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math>, mas a WAN despacha cada pacote em apenas <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0{,}6\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math>. Quando o pacote seguinte chega da LAN ao router, a WAN já acabou de enviar o anterior há <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0{,}2\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math> e está livre à espera!</p>\n<p>Instantes em milissegundos (ms) em que cada pacote acaba de ser processado em cada ponto:</p>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 20%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 20%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 20%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 20%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 20%\" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">pacote</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">acaba de sair de T1</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">acaba de chegar a R1</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">acaba de sair de R1</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">acaba de chegar a T2</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">0,8</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">0,8001</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">0,8001 + 0,6 = 1,4001</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1,4001 + 15 = 16,4001</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1,6</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1,6001</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1,6001 + 0,6 = 2,2001</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2,2001 + 15 = 17,2001</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">3</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2,4</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2,4001</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2,4001 + 0,6 = 3,0001</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">3,0001 + 15 = 18,0001</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">4</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">3,2</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">3,2001</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">3,2001 + 0,6 = 3,8001</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">3,8001 + 15 = <strong>18,8001</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> a ligação mais lenta dita o ritmo; vê se há fila no router.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#vários-pacotes-e-ligações-em-série\" target=\"_blank\">📖 Vários pacotes e ligações em\nsérie</a>"],
  ["Teste · Modelo 1", "M1.11d", "<b>P. 11 (4,5 valores)</b> Rede com comutação de pacotes <i>store-and-forward</i>: <b>T1 —LAN— R1 —WAN— T2</b>. Pacotes de 1000 Bytes (com cabeçalhos) de T1 para T2. Ambas as ligações em fibra (propagação a 2×10<sup>8</sup> m/s). A LAN tem 20 m e 10 Mbit/s. Na WAN, o atraso de propagação é 15 ms e o de transmissão é 0,6 ms.<br><br>(d) Quanto demora a enviar esses <b>4 pacotes</b> de T1 para T2?", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p><strong>Significado de todas as variáveis e abreviações do problema:</strong> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Length</em> = tamanho do pacote)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> Bytes</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8000</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1000\\text{ Bytes} = 1000 \\times 8\\text{ bits} = 8000\\text{ bits} = 8\\times 10^3\\text{ b}</annotation></semantics></math>. <em>(Atenção: 1 Byte tem 8 bits; as contas de transmissão usam sempre bits, nunca Bytes!).</em> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_{LAN}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Rate</em> = taxa de transmissão / capacidade da ligação LAN)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> Mbit/s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bit/s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b/s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">10\\text{ Mbit/s} = 10 \\times 10^6\\text{ bit/s} = 10^7\\text{ b/s}</annotation></semantics></math>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">l_{LAN}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>length</em> = comprimento físico do cabo da LAN)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>20</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> metros</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">20\\text{ metros}</annotation></semantics></math>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>velocity</em> = velocidade de propagação da luz no meio físico)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\times 10^8\\text{ m/s}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(valor típico da velocidade da luz dentro do núcleo de fibra ótica)</em>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>transmission delay</em> = atraso de transmissão)</strong>: tempo que a placa de rede demora a “injetar” (empurrar) todos os bits do pacote para o cabo. Fórmula: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans} = L / R</annotation></semantics></math>. <em>(Depende do tamanho do pacote <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</annotation></semantics></math> e da taxa <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math>; não depende da distância!).</em> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>propagation delay</em> = atraso de propagação)</strong>: tempo que o sinal eletromagnético demora a percorrer fisicamente o cabo da origem ao destino à velocidade da luz. Fórmula: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">distância</mtext><mi>/</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop} = \\text{distância} / v</annotation></semantics></math>. <em>(Depende da distância e do meio; não depende do tamanho do pacote!).</em> * <strong>Dados da ligação WAN (já calculados e fornecidos no enunciado):</strong> * <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,WAN} = 0{,}6\\text{ ms} = 6\\times 10^{-4}\\text{ s}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(atraso de transmissão na WAN)</em>. * <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop,WAN} = 15\\text{ ms} = 1{,}5\\times 10^{-2}\\text{ s}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(atraso de propagação na WAN)</em>.</p>\n<p><strong>Conceito de <em>Pipelining</em> (cadeia de transmissão):</strong> Não precisamos de calcular tudo do zero para cada pacote. O ritmo de toda a rede é ditado pela <strong>ligação mais lenta (gargalo = LAN)</strong>. * A LAN transmite os 4 pacotes colados, um a seguir ao outro, demorando <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4 \\times d_{trans,LAN} = 4 \\times 0{,}8\\text{ ms} = 3{,}2\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math>. * O 4.º pacote (o último) sai de T1 ao instante <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3{,}2\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math>. A partir daí, basta cronometrar o resto do percurso deste último pacote até chegar ao destino T2 (exatamente como se estivesse sozinho): * Propagação na LAN: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0001</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop,LAN} = 0{,}0001\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math>. * Transmissão na WAN: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,WAN} = 0{,}6\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math>. * Propagação na WAN: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop,WAN} = 15\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{total,4} = 4 \\times d_{trans,LAN} + d_{prop,LAN} + d_{trans,WAN} + d_{prop,WAN}</annotation></semantics></math> <math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0001</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟏𝟖</mn><mo mathvariant=\"bold\">,</mo><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟖𝟎𝟎𝟏</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"bold\"> 𝐦𝐬</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">= 3{,}2\\text{ ms} + 0{,}0001\\text{ ms} + 0{,}6\\text{ ms} + 15\\text{ ms} = \\mathbf{18{,}8001\\text{ ms}} \\approx 18{,}8\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p>É a resolução oficial (<code>Testes/Teste_Modelo_1_resolucao.pdf</code>), com os mesmos valores. O oficial desenha o diagrama à mão e não faz a tabela: no teste basta o desenho, com os quatro atrasos assinalados.</p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> N pacotes: N × trans da ligação mais lenta + o resto do caminho de um pacote.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#vários-pacotes-e-ligações-em-série\" target=\"_blank\">📖 Vários pacotes e ligações em\nsérie</a>"],
  ["Teste · Modelo 1", "M1.12a", "<b>P. 12 (3,5 valores)</b> Um computador está ligado à Internet a 80 Mbit/s. A página está num servidor com atraso de propagação de 30 ms e tem um HTML de 10 kByte e 2 imagens de 200 kByte cada. O browser nunca abre conexões simultâneas para o mesmo servidor. Transmissão nula para as mensagens HTTP sem ficheiros; ignora o overhead das camadas abaixo da aplicação.<br><br>(a) Desenha o MSC (diagrama de sequência de mensagens) da obtenção da página (HTML + imagens) com HTTP 1.1 <b>persistente sem pipelining</b>. Faz no papel e compara.", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p><strong>Significado de todas as variáveis e abreviações:</strong> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>propagation delay</em> = atraso de propagação só de ida)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>30</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">30\\text{ ms} = 3\\times 10^{-2}\\text{ s}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(tempo que um sinal elétrico/luz demora a ir do cliente ao servidor)</em>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">RTT</mtext><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\text{RTT}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Round-Trip Time</em> = tempo de ida e volta)</strong>: tempo que um pacote pequeno demora a ir até ao servidor e a confirmação a voltar. Como a ida demora <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop}</annotation></semantics></math> e a volta demora <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop}</annotation></semantics></math>, temos: <math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">RTT</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>30</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\text{RTT} = 2 \\times d_{prop} = 2 \\times 30\\text{ ms} = 60\\text{ ms} = 6\\times 10^{-2}\\text{ s}</annotation></semantics></math> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Rate</em> = taxa de transmissão / capacidade da ligação do utilizador)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>80</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> Mbit/s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bit/s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b/s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">80\\text{ Mbit/s} = 80 \\times 10^6\\text{ bit/s} = 8\\times 10^7\\text{ b/s}</annotation></semantics></math>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L_{HTML}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Length</em> = tamanho do ficheiro HTML base)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> kByte</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">10\\text{ kByte} = 10 \\times 8 \\times 10^3\\text{ bits} = 8\\times 10^4\\text{ bits}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(1 Byte = 8 bits)</em>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,HTML}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>atraso de transmissão do HTML</em>)</strong>: tempo que a ligação demora a escoar os bits do HTML: <math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b</mtext></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟏</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"bold\"> 𝐦𝐬</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,HTML} = \\frac{L_{HTML}}{R} = \\frac{8\\times 10^4\\text{ b}}{8\\times 10^7\\text{ b/s}} = 10^{-3}\\text{ s} = \\mathbf{1\\text{ ms}}</annotation></semantics></math> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L_{img}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Length</em> = tamanho de cada uma das 2 imagens)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>200</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> kByte</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">200\\text{ kByte} = 200 \\times 8 \\times 10^3\\text{ bits} = 1{,}6\\times 10^6\\text{ bits}</annotation></semantics></math>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,img}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>atraso de transmissão de cada imagem</em>)</strong>: <math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b</mtext></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟐𝟎</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"bold\"> 𝐦𝐬</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,img} = \\frac{L_{img}}{R} = \\frac{1{,}6\\times 10^6\\text{ b}}{8\\times 10^7\\text{ b/s}} = 2\\times 10^{-2}\\text{ s} = \\mathbf{20\\text{ ms}}</annotation></semantics></math> * <strong>HTTP/1.1 persistente sem <em>pipelining</em></strong>: * <em>Persistente</em>: abre a conexão TCP apenas <strong>uma vez</strong> para todos os objetos (não precisa de abrir e fechar novas conexões para cada imagem). * <em>Sem pipelining</em>: o browser só envia o pedido do objeto seguinte <strong>depois de ter recebido completamente</strong> a resposta do objeto anterior (nunca há dois pedidos em voo ao mesmo tempo).</p>\n<p><img src=\"assets/guia-redes/sol_m1_http_msc.svg\" alt=\"Uma conexão TCP para tudo; cada pedido só sai quando a resposta anterior acabou de chegar\" /></p>\n<p><strong>Construção passo a passo do MSC (Message Sequence Chart):</strong> 1. <strong>Abertura da conexão TCP (Handshake):</strong> * O cliente envia <code>SYN</code> para o servidor (demora <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> RTT</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ RTT} = d_{prop}</annotation></semantics></math>). * O servidor responde com <code>SYN-ACK</code> (demora <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> RTT</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ RTT} = d_{prop}</annotation></semantics></math>). * Total do handshake: <strong>1 RTT</strong>. 2. <strong>Pedido e resposta do HTML:</strong> * O cliente envia o <code>ACK</code> final do handshake juntamente com o pedido <code>GET /index.html</code>. * O servidor recebe o pedido e devolve a resposta com o ficheiro HTML (demora 1 RTT de ida e volta, mais o tempo de transmissão física do ficheiro: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,HTML} = 1\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math>). 3. <strong>Descoberta das imagens:</strong> * O browser lê o ficheiro HTML que acabou de chegar e descobre que a página referencia duas imagens (<code>img1.jpg</code> e <code>img2.jpg</code>). 4. <strong>Obtenção da Imagem 1:</strong> * Envia <code>GET /img1.jpg</code>. A resposta chega 1 RTT depois e demora <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,img} = 20\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math> a passar pelo cabo. 5. <strong>Obtenção da Imagem 2 (sem pipelining):</strong> * Só quando a Imagem 1 acabou de ser recebida na totalidade é que o browser envia <code>GET /img2.jpg</code>. Demora outro 1 RTT de ida e volta mais <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,img} = 20\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math> de transmissão.</p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> 1 RTT para abrir a conexão; depois 1 RTT + transmissão por objeto, um de cada vez.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#conexões-não-persistentes-e-persistentes\" target=\"_blank\">📖 Conexões não\npersistentes e persistentes</a>"],
  ["Teste · Modelo 1", "M1.12b", "<b>P. 12 (3,5 valores)</b> Um computador está ligado à Internet a 80 Mbit/s. A página está num servidor com atraso de propagação de 30 ms e tem um HTML de 10 kByte e 2 imagens de 200 kByte cada. O browser nunca abre conexões simultâneas para o mesmo servidor. Transmissão nula para as mensagens HTTP sem ficheiros; ignora o overhead das camadas abaixo da aplicação.<br><br>(b) Com base no MSC, calcula quanto tempo demora a obter a página com as imagens.", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p><strong>Significado de todas as variáveis e abreviações:</strong> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>propagation delay</em> = atraso de propagação só de ida)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>30</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">30\\text{ ms} = 3\\times 10^{-2}\\text{ s}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(tempo que um sinal elétrico/luz demora a ir do cliente ao servidor)</em>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">RTT</mtext><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\text{RTT}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Round-Trip Time</em> = tempo de ida e volta)</strong>: tempo que um pacote pequeno demora a ir até ao servidor e a confirmação a voltar. Como a ida demora <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop}</annotation></semantics></math> e a volta demora <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop}</annotation></semantics></math>, temos: <math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">RTT</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>30</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\text{RTT} = 2 \\times d_{prop} = 2 \\times 30\\text{ ms} = 60\\text{ ms} = 6\\times 10^{-2}\\text{ s}</annotation></semantics></math> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Rate</em> = taxa de transmissão / capacidade da ligação do utilizador)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>80</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> Mbit/s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bit/s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b/s</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">80\\text{ Mbit/s} = 80 \\times 10^6\\text{ bit/s} = 8\\times 10^7\\text{ b/s}</annotation></semantics></math>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L_{HTML}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Length</em> = tamanho do ficheiro HTML base)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> kByte</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">10\\text{ kByte} = 10 \\times 8 \\times 10^3\\text{ bits} = 8\\times 10^4\\text{ bits}</annotation></semantics></math> <em>(1 Byte = 8 bits)</em>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,HTML}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>atraso de transmissão do HTML</em>)</strong>: tempo que a ligação demora a escoar os bits do HTML: <math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b</mtext></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟏</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"bold\"> 𝐦𝐬</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,HTML} = \\frac{L_{HTML}}{R} = \\frac{8\\times 10^4\\text{ b}}{8\\times 10^7\\text{ b/s}} = 10^{-3}\\text{ s} = \\mathbf{1\\text{ ms}}</annotation></semantics></math> * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L_{img}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>Length</em> = tamanho de cada uma das 2 imagens)</strong>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>200</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> kByte</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> bits</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">200\\text{ kByte} = 200 \\times 8 \\times 10^3\\text{ bits} = 1{,}6\\times 10^6\\text{ bits}</annotation></semantics></math>. * <strong><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,img}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em>atraso de transmissão de cada imagem</em>)</strong>: <math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b</mtext></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> b/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟐𝟎</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"bold\"> 𝐦𝐬</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,img} = \\frac{L_{img}}{R} = \\frac{1{,}6\\times 10^6\\text{ b}}{8\\times 10^7\\text{ b/s}} = 2\\times 10^{-2}\\text{ s} = \\mathbf{20\\text{ ms}}</annotation></semantics></math> * <strong>HTTP/1.1 persistente sem <em>pipelining</em></strong>: * <em>Persistente</em>: abre a conexão TCP apenas <strong>uma vez</strong> para todos os objetos (não precisa de abrir e fechar novas conexões para cada imagem). * <em>Sem pipelining</em>: o browser só envia o pedido do objeto seguinte <strong>depois de ter recebido completamente</strong> a resposta do objeto anterior (nunca há dois pedidos em voo ao mesmo tempo).</p>\n<p>Pelo diagrama temporal, o tempo total é a soma de todos os RTTs gastos e das transmissões dos ficheiros: * <strong>1 RTT</strong> para abrir a conexão TCP; * <strong>1 RTT</strong> para pedir e receber o início do HTML; * <strong>1 RTT</strong> para pedir e receber a Imagem 1; * <strong>1 RTT</strong> para pedir e receber a Imagem 2; * Mais os tempos de transmissão dos dados úteis (<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{trans,HTML}</annotation></semantics></math> e <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2 \\times d_{trans,img}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">RTT</mtext><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{total} = 4\\,\\text{RTT} + d_{trans,HTML} + 2\\,d_{trans,img}</annotation></semantics></math> <math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>60</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>20</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>40</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">𝟐𝟖𝟏</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"bold\"> 𝐦𝐬</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{total} = 4 \\times (60\\text{ ms}) + 1\\text{ ms} + 2 \\times (20\\text{ ms}) = 240\\text{ ms} + 1\\text{ ms} + 40\\text{ ms} = \\mathbf{281\\text{ ms}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n<p><em>(Em notação científica das potências de 10: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>81</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>281</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> ms</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">24\\times 10^{-2}\\text{ s} + 10^{-3}\\text{ s} + 4\\times 10^{-2}\\text{ s} = 2{,}81\\times 10^{-1}\\text{ s} = 281\\text{ ms}</annotation></semantics></math>).</em></p>\n<p>Fórmula geral da folha de revisão com <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=2</annotation></semantics></math> imagens em HTTP persistente sem pipelining: <math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">RTT</mtext><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> (conexão + HTML)</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">RTT</mtext><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> (uma por cada imagem)</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{total} = 2\\,\\text{RTT}\\text{ (conexão + HTML)} + n\\,\\text{RTT}\\text{ (uma por cada imagem)} + \\sum d_{trans}</annotation></semantics></math></p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> persistente sem pipelining: 2 RTT + n RTT + Σ transmissões.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#conexões-não-persistentes-e-persistentes\" target=\"_blank\">📖 Conexões não\npersistentes e persistentes</a>"],
  ["Teste · Modelo 1", "M1.13", "<b>P. 13 (2 valores)</b> Desenha as setas das mensagens DNS para resolver <b>iterativamente</b> o nome <code>www.jn.pt</code>, entre o cliente, o servidor de raiz, o servidor de topo (TLD) e o servidor com autoridade. Faz no papel e compara.", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p><strong>Conceitos e termos de DNS que precisas de saber para este exercício:</strong> * <strong>Resolução Iterativa</strong>: o cliente pergunta a um nível da hierarquia; o servidor contactado responde <em>“eu não sei o IP final, mas contacta este outro servidor mais abaixo”</em> (devolve uma referência / delegação). O cliente é quem faz as perguntas todas, uma a uma. <strong>Nenhuma seta liga dois servidores entre si.</strong> * <strong>Hierarquia dos servidores contactados:</strong> 1. <strong>Servidor de Raiz (<em>Root</em>)</strong>: conhece os servidores dos TLDs (<code>.pt</code>, <code>.com</code>). 2. <strong>Servidor TLD (<em>Top-Level Domain</em>, <code>.pt</code>)</strong>: conhece os servidores autoritários de cada domínio em Portugal (<code>jn.pt</code>, <code>up.pt</code>). 3. <strong>Servidor com Autoridade (<em>Authoritative Server</em>, <code>jn.pt</code>)</strong>: guarda a base de dados oficial com os IPs do Jornal de Notícias. * <strong>Tipos de registos referidos:</strong> * <strong>Registo NS (<em>Name Server</em>)</strong>: indica o nome do servidor de nomes com autoridade para um domínio. * <strong>Registo A (<em>Address</em>)</strong>: indica o endereço IPv4 definitivo da máquina pedida. * <strong>Flag <code>aa</code> (<em>Authoritative Answer</em>)</strong>: indica que a resposta vem do servidor oficial dono do domínio e não de uma cópia em cache.</p>\n<p><img src=\"assets/guia-redes/sol_m1_dns_iterativo.svg\" alt=\"Resolução iterativa: o cliente pergunta a cada nível e cada um devolve só a referência para o seguinte\" /></p>\n<p>São <strong>6 mensagens</strong> (3 pares de pedido/resposta), sempre entre o cliente (na prática, o servidor de nomes local) e um servidor de cada vez:</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Mensagem 1 (Cliente <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math> Servidor de Raiz):</strong> “Qual é o registo A (endereço IP) de <code>www.jn.pt</code>?”</li>\n<li><strong>Mensagem 2 (Servidor de Raiz <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math> Cliente):</strong> Não tem o IP, mas devolve os <strong>registos NS do TLD <code>pt</code></strong> (e os respetivos IPs na secção adicional, para o cliente saber como contactar o TLD).</li>\n<li><strong>Mensagem 3 (Cliente <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math> Servidor TLD <code>pt</code>):</strong> “Qual é o registo A de <code>www.jn.pt</code>?”</li>\n<li><strong>Mensagem 4 (Servidor TLD <code>pt</code> <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math> Cliente):</strong> Não tem o IP da máquina, mas devolve os <strong>registos NS do domínio <code>jn.pt</code></strong> (o servidor com autoridade).</li>\n<li><strong>Mensagem 5 (Cliente <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math> Servidor com Autoridade de <code>jn.pt</code>):</strong> “Qual é o registo A de <code>www.jn.pt</code>?”</li>\n<li><strong>Mensagem 6 (Servidor com Autoridade <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mo>→</mo><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math> Cliente):</strong> Resposta conclusiva: devolve o <strong>registo A com o IP final</strong> de <code>www.jn.pt</code> (com a flag <code>aa = 1</code>).</li>\n</ol>\n<p><em>(No teste: desenha as 6 setas tal como na figura e escreve junto de cada uma o que leva — por exemplo: “1: GET A www.jn.pt”, “2: NS pt”, “3: GET A www.jn.pt”, “4: NS jn.pt”, “5: GET A www.jn.pt”, “6: A IP-final”).</em></p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> iterativo: o cliente pergunta a cada nível; nenhuma seta entre servidores.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#hierarquia-de-servidores\" target=\"_blank\">📖 Hierarquia de servidores</a>"],
];
